    "note": "The rule-of-three 'Nothing.' running gag escalates well. Wren's rant gets more absurd each time (the sun and earth shot), and the 7-2 reveal, crickets and scream land the payoff. The poker is legal and plausible: KK folds to a river shove on a dry board, and 7♣2♦ has no pair, straight or flush, so it really is air. The one nitpick is that the AI wouldn't have to show its hand. The hook title 'POV:' plus the 'bluffs with pure air' line is decent but a bit abstract, and the opening table shot is static. A punchier first frame, such as the shove or Wren's folded kings, would stop the scroll faster. The CTA in the caption ('Think you can read a bluff?') fits the brand, and the deadpan CHIP gives the AI a fun personality."
